(7562246, 1212303, 185714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 3DsArcher:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nicely captured. Possibly a slightly slower shutter speed would of blurred the propellors for a more natural look but a cracking image all the same </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As much as I wanted like u mentioned, but the planes are super fast.  If i slower the shutter speed, I may get the both planes blur.  BUT, I can try next time as suggested.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your feedback.<br/> <br/>/gin</td>', 'Originally posted by 3DsArcher: Very nicely captured. Possibly a slightly slower shutter speed would of blurred the propellors for a more natural look but a cracking image all the same   As much as I wanted like u mentioned, but the planes are super fast.  If i slower the shutter speed, I may get the both planes blur.  BUT, I can try next time as suggested. Thank you for your feedback. /gin', '2018-03-08 21:45:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7562247, 1212303, 185714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pgirish007:</b></div><hr/><i> I was the only one who rated this 9 as to me it was well taken and does show that they are flying and at an interesting angles! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you so much for your vote &amp; comments.<br/> <br/>Is a tough &amp; great shoot.  Handling Sigma 150-600 lens swinging from left to right vice versa, is a pain in the neck lol.  <br/> <br/>cheers<br/>gin<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by pgirish007: I was the only one who rated this 9 as to me it was well taken and does show that they are flying and at an interesting angles!   Thank you so much for your vote & comments. Is a tough & great shoot.  Handling Sigma 150-600 lens swinging from left to right vice versa, is a pain in the neck lol.   cheersgin ', '2018-03-08 21:48:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7562390, 1212370, 100831, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get the title but I do like the photo and the unanswered questions and edginess. I gave it a 6 on first pass, had I reviewed it I think I would have gone to 7.</td>', 'I didn''t get the title but I do like the photo and the unanswered questions and edginess. I gave it a 6 on first pass, had I reviewed it I think I would have gone to 7.', '2018-03-10 12:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7562391, 1212370, 2158, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t get the title but I do like the photo and the unanswered questions and edginess. I gave it a 6 on first pass, had I reviewed it I think I would have gone to 7. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The title refers to the girl they''re looking at - the subject outside the frame. And yes, there was a girl. I even have the photo to prove it.</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyStreet: I didn''t get the title but I do like the photo and the unanswered questions and edginess. I gave it a 6 on first pass, had I reviewed it I think I would have gone to 7.   The title refers to the girl they''re looking at - the subject outside the frame. And yes, there was a girl. I even have the photo to prove it.', '2018-03-10 12:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
